WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.494 --> 00:00:19.995
Gerald didn't know what to say to the Ugly-Wugly.

2
00:00:20.015 --> 00:00:22.477
"You want a hotel?"

3
00:00:22.937 --> 00:00:23.898
he finally said.

4
00:00:23.918 --> 00:00:27.941
"A good hotel," said the middle-aged gentleman.

5
00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:32.304
"I'm sorry, but the hotels here shut early.

6
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:33.881
They're all closed now."

7
00:00:34.882 --> 00:00:37.464
Gerald had said the first thing that came into his head.

8
00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:41.527
He couldn't send these creatures to a real hotel.

9
00:00:42.488 --> 00:00:44.029
They'd frighten everyone in town!

10
00:00:44.049 --> 00:00:46.932
"What about a lodging house?"

11
00:00:47.412 --> 00:00:48.673
asked a lady in a bonnet.

12
00:00:49.734 --> 00:00:52.216
Another lady pushed her way to the front of the group.

13
00:00:52.236 --> 00:00:55.339
"Where are the carriages that we ordered?"

14
00:00:55.359 --> 00:01:01.604
"I don't know, but I'll find out," said Gerald, pretending everything was normal.

15
00:01:02.928 --> 00:01:04.049
"We'd better get going now.

16
00:01:04.329 --> 00:01:05.249
The play is over.

17
00:01:05.789 --> 00:01:07.910
It's time to close the building and put out the lights."

18
00:01:09.611 --> 00:01:13.793
"Let's get going," repeated the gentleman, who seemed to be the leader of the group.

19
00:01:14.773 --> 00:01:16.154
He stepped toward the front door.

20
00:01:23.017 --> 00:01:26.558
can go with you and help you find a place to stay," said Gerald.

21
00:01:26.578 --> 00:01:30.000
"But you'll have to wait a few moments in the backyard."

22
00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:32.505
The Ugly-Wuglies grumbled.

23
00:01:33.425 --> 00:01:35.626
For some reason they didn't like that idea.

24
00:01:35.646 --> 00:01:41.088
"It's a very nice backyard," Gerald said.

25
00:01:41.108 --> 00:01:43.849
"The pump was just painted green."

26
00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:47.451
The Ugly-Wuglies seemed interested in the fresh paint.

27
00:01:49.732 --> 00:01:51.693
Gerald led them out into the backyard.

28
00:01:53.473 --> 00:01:54.994
He hoped no one would see them.

29
00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:59.896
"I hate to make you wait," he said, inventing an excuse.

30
00:02:01.232 --> 00:02:02.913
"But my uncle is quite insane.

31
00:02:03.353 --> 00:02:04.794
I have to give him his supper now.

32
00:02:05.354 --> 00:02:10.016
When he sees strangers—even nice ones like you—he gets quite upset.

33
00:02:10.416 --> 00:02:11.757
So please wait right here."

34
00:02:13.097 --> 00:02:16.039
"Perhaps we should try to find a hotel ourselves?"

35
00:02:16.619 --> 00:02:18.660
the lady in the bonnet said nervously.

36
00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:22.962
"Oh no," Gerald said, acting very serious.

37
00:02:23.962 --> 00:02:25.783
"The police arrest all strangers.

38
00:02:26.344 --> 00:02:27.204
It's a new law."

39
00:02:28.752 --> 00:02:32.153
As Gerald went back into the school, he heard the creatures muttering.

40
00:02:33.113 --> 00:02:36.234
They said things like "quite the polite young gentleman."

41
00:02:37.174 --> 00:02:40.535
Although the creatures looked horrible, Gerald wasn't afraid.

42
00:02:41.555 --> 00:02:43.696
He knew it was because he was wearing the ring.

43
00:02:44.896 --> 00:02:47.377
As long as he didn't touch them, he could be brave.

44
00:02:51.298 --> 00:02:53.519
He found the other children in the dining room.

45
00:02:54.419 --> 00:02:55.959
He didn't want them to be afraid.

46
00:02:55.979 --> 00:02:58.160
"This is such fun!"

47
00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:00.301
he said in a cheerful voice.

48
00:03:00.321 --> 00:03:03.724
"The Ugly-Wuglies are just like real people.

49
00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:05.905
They're quite kind and jolly."

50
00:03:05.925 --> 00:03:09.708
"Fun?" Kathleen said doubtfully.

51
00:03:11.009 --> 00:03:13.331
Gerald told them about the need for a hotel.

52
00:03:13.351 --> 00:03:17.714
"Wait here while I go up to talk to Mademoiselle and Eliza."

53
00:03:20.115 --> 00:03:21.116
He ran upstairs.

54
00:03:21.136 --> 00:03:26.300
"I wonder what lies he's telling them," said Jimmy.

55
00:03:28.272 --> 00:03:31.473
Gerald came down again and said that he'd walk Mabel home.

56
00:03:31.493 --> 00:03:36.474
"What about a hotel for the Ugly-Wuglies?"

57
00:03:36.974 --> 00:03:37.755
she reminded him.

58
00:03:37.775 --> 00:03:40.856
"Is there a place on the castle grounds?

59
00:03:41.316 --> 00:03:44.937
I need to put them somewhere until the charm breaks," said Gerald.

60
00:03:48.958 --> 00:03:50.878
they'll just be a pack of coats and things.

61
00:03:51.278 --> 00:03:52.759
And we can carry those home later."

62
00:03:52.779 --> 00:03:58.153
"There's a secret passage in the Temple of Flora," said Mabel.

63
00:03:59.974 --> 00:04:02.376
Right then an Ugly-Wugly opened the back door.

64
00:04:03.217 --> 00:04:04.358
He looked in anxiously.

65
00:04:04.378 --> 00:04:08.241
"We'd better go," said Gerald.

66
00:04:09.222 --> 00:04:10.643
He went outside with Mabel.

67
00:04:10.663 --> 00:04:13.045
"This is my friend Mabel.

68
00:04:13.485 --> 00:04:15.027
She played the princess in the play."

69
00:04:17.208 --> 00:04:19.490
The middle-aged Ugly-Wugly shook her hand.

70
00:04:20.471 --> 00:04:22.473
The one in the bonnet took Mabel's arm.

71
00:04:22.493 --> 00:04:24.534
"You clever thing.

72
00:04:24.975 --> 00:04:26.016
Do walk with me."

73
00:04:28.144 --> 00:04:31.245
And so they walked through town like any other group of people.

74
00:04:32.226 --> 00:04:35.307
Mabel had to keep telling herself that the creatures weren't real.

75
00:04:39.929 --> 00:04:42.470
They passed only one man who stared at them.

76
00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:45.071
But he just muttered to himself.

77
00:04:47.872 --> 00:04:50.493
At last they reached the gates to the castle grounds.

78
00:04:51.514 --> 00:04:53.935
Gerald tried to open the gates, but couldn't.

79
00:04:54.775 --> 00:04:55.655
They were locked.
